> Hand-check triangular RGB mean coupling

For a given component, coefficients are alpha=tanh(cRG), beta=tanh(cBR),
gamma=tanh(cBG). The teacher-forced conditional means are

$$ m_R=\mu_R,\quad m_G=\mu_G+\alpha x_R,\quad
m_B=\mu_B+\beta x_R+\gamma x_G. $$
\alttext(Green's mean depends on observed red; blue's mean depends on observed red and green. Red's mean has no within-pixel input.)

The RGB component log probability is the sum of its three conditional channel
log masses. Add normalized mixture log weights and apply stable logsumexp over
components. Its stabilizing maximum is stopped; applicable first and higher
paths through the mixture remain live. The model loss averages joint RGB pixel
NLL and divides by three, so it is **nats per RGB channel**. Image joint NLLs
instead sum all64 RGB pixel NLLs without dividing by three.

Set base means to zero and(alpha,beta,gamma)=(.5,.25,−.75). Hold observed green
at.4 and vary observed red. Then mG=.5R and mB=.25R−.3. These continuous toy
inputs check the live formula; real observations later use exact byte centers.
During generation, replace the observed R/G by already **sampled and quantized**
R/G. Replacing them with unquantized draws or with component means changes the
source model's sampling distribution.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pp_coupling_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;auto t=n::DType::Float64;
 auto r=n::tensor({-1.,-.5,0.,.5,1.},{5,1},t);auto x=n::concat({r,n::full({5,1},.4,t),n::zeros({5,1},t)},1);
 std::vector<double> row(10);row[7]=std::atanh(.5);row[8]=std::atanh(.25);row[9]=std::atanh(-.75);
 auto p=n::tile(n::from_vector(row,{1,10}),{5,1}).requires_grad_();
 auto o=n::models::DiscretizedLogisticRGB(x,p,1);auto means=n::reshape(o.means,{5,3});
 auto green=n::slice_axis(means,1,1,2),blue=n::slice_axis(means,1,2,3);
 if(n::max(n::abs(green-.5*r)).item()>1e-14||n::max(n::abs(blue-(.25*r-.3))).item()>1e-14)throw std::runtime_error("Coupling identity");
 auto g=n::grad(o.mean_channel_nll,{p})[0];
 if(n::max(n::abs(n::slice_axis(g,1,7,10))).item()==0)throw std::runtime_error("Coupling path");
 dm::graphics::RPlot::create().lines(r.to_vector<double>(),green.to_vector<double>(),"Green mean given R",{22,163,74})
 .lines(r.to_vector<double>(),blue.to_vector<double>(),"Blue mean given R,G=.4",{37,99,235})
 .y_limits(-.7,1.05).x_label("Observed red value").y_label("Coupled conditional mean")
 .title("Observed channels couple only forward through RGB").save_svg("build/pp_coupling_toy.svg");
}
