> Trace the actual compact context architecture

There are1410 stored values in23 ordered leaves,962 active and448 structurally
masked. Kernels initialize normal(.1), biases zero, using native seed8609.
The following diagram is traced from the executable context, not from invented
layer dimensions. The30-channel head is component-major. Its parameters do not
see current R/G; those dependencies arise only in the separately evaluated
likelihood. No hidden optimizer or training loop is part of either native call.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pp_network.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;n::ParameterStore p(8609);
 n::Module model([&](const n::Tensor& x){
  auto o=n::models::GatedPixelConvolutional(p,x,n::Tensor(),false,3,30);
  n::model_stage("Block0 vertical gate",x,o.vertical0);
  n::model_stage("Block0 horizontal",std::vector<n::Tensor>{x,o.vertical0},o.horizontal0);
  n::model_stage("Block1 vertical gate",o.vertical0,o.vertical1);
  n::model_stage("Block1 horizontal residual",std::vector<n::Tensor>{o.horizontal0,o.vertical1},o.horizontal1);
  n::model_stage("Block2 vertical gate",o.vertical1,o.vertical);
  n::model_stage("Block2 horizontal residual",std::vector<n::Tensor>{o.horizontal1,o.vertical},o.horizontal);
  return n::model_stage("1x1 head:3 components x10",o.horizontal,o.logits);
 },"Compact RGB context:1410 stored /962 active values");
 n::ModelPlotOptions options;options.detail=n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;options.sizing.minimum_extent=2;options.sizing.max_planes=4;
 auto fig=model.plot(n::zeros({1,8,8,3}),options);
 if(fig.parameter_count()!=1410||p.size()!=23)throw std::runtime_error("Source census");
 fig.save_svg("build/pp_network.svg");
}
```
