> Keep extreme likelihood fixtures and endpoint normalization visible

The original normalization fixture enumerates all256 byte centers for each of
three components and three channels. It includes logits(−80,0,80), means
(−2,0,2) and log scales(−7,−.3,3), with zero coupling. Every channel/component
mass sums to one within2e−5. An additional eight-case fixture includes both
endpoint bins, nonzero coupling and raw scales below−7. All saved likelihood
fields and all fixture parameter partials are finite. The source archive and
the independent oracle retain every case; none is silently dropped as a tail.

The CDF plot below displays all256 bins for each component's red-channel
fixture. Green and blue have the same uncoupled parameters in this specific
normalization fixture; all nine distributions are checked numerically.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pp_normalization.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;n::Tensor mass;for(auto& [k,v]:n::load_npz("build/pixel_cnn_pp/normalization.npz"))if(k=="channel_log_mass")mass=n::exp(n::cast(v,n::DType::Float64));
 auto sums=n::sum(mass,{0});if(n::max(n::abs(sums-1)).item()>2e-5)throw std::runtime_error("Nine distributions");
 auto cumulative=n::cumsum(mass,0),x=n::arange(0,256);auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
 const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colours{{220,38,38},{37,99,235},{22,163,74}};
 for(int component=0;component<3;++component){auto y=n::select(n::select(cumulative,1,component),1,0);
  plot.lines(x.to_vector<double>(),y.to_vector<double>(),"Component "+std::to_string(component+1),colours[component]);}
 plot.y_limits(-.02,1.6).x_label("8-bit code").y_label("Cumulative channel probability")
 .title("All endpoint tails remain in each categorical distribution").save_svg("build/pp_normalization.svg");
 std::print("Nine full256-bin distributions; max mass-sum error {:.3g}.\n",n::max(n::abs(sums-1)).item());
}
