> Compare the fixed final loss with fitting-only baselines

The histogram baseline estimates a separate256-category marginal for each
channel, pooled over fitting cases and sites. It adds Jeffreys.5 to each code
count and divides by128×64+128; validation/test bytes never fit the baseline.
It ignores both spatial and within-pixel dependencies. Uniform code probabilities
cost exactly8 bits per channel. These losses concern the quantized8x8 observation
space, so they cannot be compared directly with published32x32 CIFAR likelihoods.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pp_history.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
