> Preserve the observed top half in every completion

Each row is truth / observed top half / generated completion for one of the
first six test cases. All96 observed channel codes (32 whole pixels) per image
are preserved exactly. Unknowns are signed zero only in the middle presentation
panel, rendered gray; the sampler starts its unknown canvas at zero and never
copies hidden truth into it. Completion cannot read lower-half truth through
its head masks. All cases and raw banks are retained, not selected by appearance.

