> Inspect mixture choices without assigning semantic labels to components

For the24 generated images, compare mean conditional component weights across
all1536 sampled pixels with empirical component-choice frequencies. The heads
change with the generated prefix, so the mean weights describe this adaptive
sample pool, not a fixed independent multinomial experiment or calibrated class
probabilities. Component indices have no supervised semantic identity and could
be permuted together with their parameters without changing the density.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pp_components.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;std::map<std::string,n::Tensor> a;for(auto& [k,v]:n::load_npz("build/pixel_cnn_pp/samples.npz"))a.emplace(k,v);
 auto params=n::reshape(n::cast(a.at("parameters"),n::DType::Float64),{24,64,3,10});
 auto logits=n::select(params,3,0);auto weights=n::softmax(logits,2);
 auto expected=n::mean(weights,{0,1}),observed=n::mean(n::one_hot(a.at("components"),3,1,0,n::DType::Float64),{0,1});
 if(std::abs(n::sum(expected).item()-1)>1e-12||std::abs(n::sum(observed).item()-1)>1e-12)throw std::runtime_error("Mixture frequency normalization");
 dm::graphics::RPlot::create().points({1,2,3},expected.to_vector<double>(),"Mean conditional weight",{37,99,235},6)
 .points({1,2,3},observed.to_vector<double>(),"Empirical chosen fraction",{220,38,38},4)
 .y_limits(0,1.35).x_label("Unsupervised component index").y_label("Fraction of sampled pixels")
 .title("One mixture component is selected for each whole RGB pixel").save_svg("build/pp_components.svg");
}
```
