> Audit evidence and limits

The report reproduces all24 original archives containing1223447 values and all
144 captured gradient/update/iteration archives containing135408 values,
including exact batch and history TSVs. Both original PNG galleries are checked
by decoded pixels; complete C++ programs remain editable here. The frozen source
and optional TF-reference absence are pinned in
`build/nn-report-conversion/pixel_cnn_pp/baseline.json`.

`scripts/check_pixel_cnn_pp.py` independently verifies589824 original RGB
values,36864 area-quantized channel codes,379469 forward values,78420 partials,
29 finite differences,48 Adam writes,12288 causal entries,64 future flips and
9792 sampled channel values across epoch/final/prefix draws. Every sampled code
is reproduced from independent NumPy context heads, including quantized R/G
coupling. All448 masked coordinates remain exact. The largest absolute forward
difference.001451 is an extreme-tail component log probability (scaled error
1.66e−7); maximum partial difference is7.63e−7. No independent framework runtime
or replacement fitted trajectory is needed by the report.

The canonical header `datamunge/nn/logistic_pixels.hpp` provides reusable native
preparation, likelihood and model evaluation; Python and R remain thin bindings.
Eight new native tests plus518 selected C++ tests,277 Python tests and1989 R
expectations in55 files pass. All29 new documentation definitions, six compiled
header examples, six clangd hovers and checkout/installed standalone headers
pass. That evidence establishes implementation and migration fidelity. The tiny
source pools, fixed three-epoch endpoint and unfiltered visual results support
no claim of state-of-the-art likelihood, realistic generation or generalization
to the full original-resolution CIFAR benchmark.

